---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About — WordTally"
	description="WordTally is a small, focused, client-side word and character counter. Learn what it does and why it's built this way."
	canonicalPath="/about"
>
	<section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
		<h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[#2B2013] sm:text-5xl">
			About WordTally
		</h1>

		<div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-[#5C4F3D]">
			<p>
				WordTally is a single-purpose writing tool: a live word, character,
				and sentence counter with reading time, speaking time, and keyword
				density, all in one clean page.
			</p>
			<p>
				We built it deliberately small. Rather than bundling dozens of
				unrelated utilities into one bloated site, WordTally does one job
				and does it well &mdash; count and analyze your text instantly, with
				no clutter and no distractions.
			</p>
			<p>
				Everything runs entirely in your browser. There is no upload, no
				account, and no server processing your text. When you close the tab,
				nothing you typed persists anywhere.
			</p>
			<p>
				Reading time is calculated at 200 words per minute and speaking time
				at 130 words per minute &mdash; both commonly used averages for adult
				reading and presentation pacing. Keyword density highlights your top
				5 most-used meaningful words, filtering out common stopwords like
				&ldquo;the&rdquo;, &ldquo;and&rdquo;, and &ldquo;is&rdquo; so you can
				see what your writing actually emphasizes.
			</p>
			<p>
				WordTally is free to use, with no signup required.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
